L1 Fejer-Riesz: random nonneg trig polys of degree N-1 are |q|^2 (canonical phase densities of N-level pure states)
  N=2: 20 random nonneg polys factorized, max |p - |q|^2| = 2.78e-16
  N=3: 20 random nonneg polys factorized, max |p - |q|^2| = 5.55e-16
  N=5: 20 random nonneg polys factorized, max |p - |q|^2| = 8.88e-16
  N=8: 20 random nonneg polys factorized, max |p - |q|^2| = 1.80e-15
L2 readable-information cap ln N (Nikolskii/Cauchy-Schwarz: max|q|^2 <= N * mean|q|^2)
  N=2: max ratio 1.9999 <= 2;  sine state: I_canonical=0.3069, Holevo chi=0.6931, ln N=0.6931
  N=3: max ratio 2.9901 <= 3;  sine state: I_canonical=0.6137, Holevo chi=1.0397, ln N=1.0986
  N=8: max ratio 6.1092 <= 8;  sine state: I_canonical=1.4882, Holevo chi=1.8870, ln N=2.0794
  N=32: max ratio 8.7384 <= 32;  sine state: I_canonical=2.8129, Holevo chi=3.1896, ln N=3.4657
L3 orbitope: shifted Fejer kernels give N perfectly distinguishable states and a partition of unity
  N=2: max|sum_i e_i - 1| = 6.7e-16; max|e_i(node_j) - delta_ij| = 3.7e-33
  N=3: max|sum_i e_i - 1| = 1.0e-15; max|e_i(node_j) - delta_ij| = 7.9e-32
  N=5: max|sum_i e_i - 1| = 1.2e-15; max|e_i(node_j) - delta_ij| = 1.8e-32
  N=9: max|sum_i e_i - 1| = 3.1e-15; max|e_i(node_j) - delta_ij| = 4.4e-31
L4 Markov clock coherence |Im|/|Re| vs cot(pi/N) (Dmitriev-Dynkin 1946; Barato-Seifert 2017; Ohga-Ito-Kolchinsky 2023)
  N=3: max sampled ratio 0.5773  vs cot(pi/N) = 0.5774
  N=4: max sampled ratio 0.9919  vs cot(pi/N) = 1.0000
  N=5: max sampled ratio 1.2991  vs cot(pi/N) = 1.3764
  N=6: max sampled ratio 1.4754  vs cot(pi/N) = 1.7321
L5 mixing finite records: for ANY estimate law, mean over theta of P(|theta - theta_hat| > pi/2) = 1/2
  N=17: mean 0.5000, max over theta 0.7673
  N=16: mean 0.5000, max over theta 0.8169
  N=9: mean 0.5000, max over theta 0.9238
  a3 N=8: tail at t=1,10,100,1000 rev: [np.float64(0.4553), np.float64(0.5), np.float64(0.5), np.float64(0.5)]
  a3 N=32: tail at t=1,10,100,1000 rev: [np.float64(0.1588), np.float64(0.4987), np.float64(0.5), np.float64(0.5)]
L6 record dimensions: quantum full N^2, orbit span (Toeplitz section) 2N-1
  N=2: rank of generic orbit span = 3 (2N-1=3, N^2=4)
  N=3: rank of generic orbit span = 5 (2N-1=5, N^2=9)
  N=5: rank of generic orbit span = 9 (2N-1=9, N^2=25)
  N=8: rank of generic orbit span = 15 (2N-1=15, N^2=64)
L7 (follow-up probe) sphere: SU(2) orbit of a spin coherent state spans all N^2 dims; band-limited count sum_{l<=N-1}(2l+1) = N^2
  N=2: rank 4  N^2=4  band-limited count=4
  N=3: rank 9  N^2=9  band-limited count=9
  N=4: rank 16  N^2=16  band-limited count=16
